<title>NETHERLANDS: Bangert Pontier raises Pakhoed to a Buy.</title>
<headline>Bangert Pontier raises Pakhoed to a Buy.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-07-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Research note summary (10/07)</p>
<p>Company-----Sector------------Price---Broker----------------</p>
<p>    Pakhoed     storage,shipping  70.50   Bank Bangert Pontier</p>
<p>COMMENT: Buy (from Hold)</p>
<p>Earnings per share estimates raised, based on ongoing strong sales in chemicals distribution and stable margins in 1998. In 1997, Pakhoed can gain from reorganisation in the U.S. and the stronger dollar. Based on our earnings per share estimates and a fair price/earnings ration of 15, we come to a price target of 90.00 guilders and we upgrade the stock from Hold to Buy.</p>
<p>    Estimates (NLG):  EPS*    pvs EPS   P/E    Dividend</p>
<p>    1996 (actual)     4.45		  12.1   1.80</p>
<p>    1997		  5.90    4.95	12.0   2.30</p>
<p>    1998		  6.70    5.35	10.5   2.50</p>
<p>    1999		  7.10    5.80	10.0   2.70</p>
<p>* NOTE - earnings per share excluding extraordinary items</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom, +31 20 504 5000 (Fax +31 20 504 5040)</p>
